Q4. String Pool (Memory Concept)
Java stores string literals in a String Constant Pool
Helps save memory by reusing objects

String s1 = "Java";
String s2 = "Java";
System.out.println(s1 == s2); // true (same memory)

But:
String s3 = new String("Java");
System.out.println(s1 == s3); // false
-------------------------------------------------
Q5. == vs equals() (MOST ASKED)
Ans:
== checks Reference (memory address)
equals() checks Content (value)

String a = "Hello";
String b = new String("Hello");

System.out.println(a == b);      // false
System.out.println(a.equals(b)); // true
- Always use equals() for content comparison.
