Q9. String vs StringBuffer vs StringBuilder
Ans:
Feature: Mutability
String: Immutable
StringBuffer: Mutable
StringBuilder: Mutable

Feature: Thread Safe
String: Yes
StringBuffer: Yes
StringBuilder: No

Feature: Performance
String: Slow
StringBuffer: Medium
StringBuilder: Fast

Feature: Use
String: Read‑only data
StringBuilder: Single‑thread performance
StringBuffer: Multi‑thread safety

StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Java");
sb.append(" World");
System.out.println(sb);
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Q10. String Interning
Ans:
Moves string to String Pool
Example:
String s1 = new String("Java");
String s2 = s1.intern();
System.out.println(s1 == s2); // false

